# Problems with Literate Programming/WEB

I really want to love the idea of Literate Programming, and the notion of writing code in a fundamentally expository manner, as well as the thought any method for programming that opens the door to greater levels of artistry/humanity—both hold great appeal for me.

But there are a number of concerns I have with Knuth's approach, and other similar methods that have followed after it.

## The formatting language isn’t terribly readable
## Major design changes require even more major reworking
## The “woven” (book) form uses unusual/confusing replacement symbols

Rather than what would actually be present in familiar C code.

## Writing a book instead of raw code, may impede achieving the “flow state”

A.k.a. being “in the zone”.

## Writing a program as an entirely self-consistent “book” demands excessive re-editing

## In many cases, unadorned code can be easier to read

